# Domain DTOs

DTOs are the stable contract between the API layer and Domain Actions. They are the only "input shapes" Actions should accept.

## Rules

- One file per DTO under `LoadlyAggregator.Domain/{Admin|Company|Driver|Contractor|Collector|Common}/DTOs/<Feature>/`.
- Use the right suffix: `CreateXDto`, `UpdateXDto`, `XDto` (read model), `ListXDto` (list input/response), or `XResponse` for action outputs that aren't a plain DTO.
- Members are **primitives, enums-as-int, other DTOs, or collections of those**. Never put an entity (`Admin`, `Invoice`, …) on a DTO.
- No methods beyond trivial `public static TDto FromEntity(TEntity e)` factories when it keeps mapping close to the data.
- No `[Required]`, no FluentValidation, no `HttpContext`. Validation is on the Request, not the DTO.
- No references to `LoadlyAggregator.API` or `LoadlyAggregator.Infrastructure`.

## Example

```csharp
public class CreateAdminDto
{
    public string FullName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string UserName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Phone { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Status { get; set; }
    public int MfaChannel { get; set; }
    public List<long>? RoleIds { get; set; }
}
```

## When to add a `XResponse` instead of reusing `XDto`

Add a dedicated `XResponse` when an Action needs to return something that isn't the normal single-entity read shape — e.g. aggregate counts, paged results plus metadata, or a composite ("login response"). Otherwise reuse the existing `XDto`.
